cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this Lean formalization, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "GMT Foundations: sets of finite perimeter, Reifenberg theorems, and Sobolev compactness in Lean"
version: "0.1.0"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/willmfeldman/gmt-foundations"
authors:
  - family-names: Feldman
    given-names: "William M."
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of the De Giorgi–Federer structure theory of sets of
  locally finite perimeter (Gauss–Green measures, De Giorgi blow-up, rectifiability of the
  essential boundary, the perimeter measure as Hausdorff measure, and the null case of
  Federer's criterion), the discrete and rectifiable Reifenberg theorems of Naber and
  Valtorta for hyperplanes, and Rellich–Kondrachov compactness with compact boundary trace.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - geometric measure theory
  - sets of finite perimeter
  - Reifenberg theorem
  - Sobolev spaces
